KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ free functions: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ static member functions: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ pointers to member functions: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ noexcept to plain pointer: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The exception specification is a comment of the function type
(#C_noexcept), which type equality ignores: a pointer to a throwing
function converted to a pointer to noexcept function, and the two
overloads of k were ambiguous.  standard_conversion_sequence now applies
[conv.fctptr] and ranks the function pointer conversion below the
identity.
